.TH man 1 "2026-11-19" "0.20.0" "Profanity XMPP client"

.SH NAME
/vcard

.SH DESCRIPTION
View or edit your vCard profile (XEP-0054). If no arguments are given, your vCard is displayed. 

.SH SYNOPSIS
/vcard

.LP
/vcard get [<nick|contact>]

.LP
/vcard edit

.LP
/vcard photo open <nick|contact> [<index>]

.LP
/vcard photo save <nick|contact> [output <filepath>] [index <index>]

.LP
/vcard photo open-self [<index>]

.LP
/vcard photo save-self [output <filepath>] [index <index>]

.LP

.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
\fBget [<nick|contact>]\fR
.RS 4
View your vCard, or a contact's vCard if provided.
.RE
.PP
\fBedit\fR
.RS 4
Edit your vCard profile in an interactive form window.
.RE
.PP
\fBphoto open <nick|contact> [<index>]\fR
.RS 4
Download a user's photo from their vCard to a file, and open it.
.RE
.PP
\fBphoto save <nick|contact>\fR
.RS 4
Download a user's photo from their vCard to a file.
.RE
.PP
\fBphoto open-self [<index>]\fR
.RS 4
Download a photo from your vCard to a file, and open it.
.RE
.PP
\fBphoto save-self\fR
.RS 4
Download a photo from your vCard to a file.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
/vcard

.LP
/vcard get

.LP
/vcard get friend@server.org

.LP
/vcard edit

.LP
/vcard photo open friend@server.org

.LP
